Orders demonstrate that embedding and referencing can be used together.

```javascript
{
  _id: "O501",
  customerId: "C102",
  status: "PAID",
  orderedAt: ISODate("2024-03-10T14:32:00Z"),

  shippingAddress: {
    city: "Seattle",
    postalCode: "98101"
  },

  items: [
    {
      productId: "P204",
      name: "MongoDB Basics",
      qty: 1,
      unitPrice: NumberDecimal("49.00")
    },
    {
      productId: "P310",
      name: "Compass Lab",
      qty: 2,
      unitPrice: NumberDecimal("19.00")
    }
  ],

  totals: {
    subtotal: NumberDecimal("87.00"),
    tax: NumberDecimal("11.31"),
    grandTotal: NumberDecimal("98.31")
  }
}
```

Avoid a product document containing every review:

```javascript
{
  _id: "P204",
  name: "MongoDB Basics",
  reviews: [
    // Could eventually contain millions of elements
  ]
}
```

Store reviews in a separate collection instead.

Avoid:

```javascript
{ price: 29.99 }
{ price: "29.99" }
{ price: { amount: 29.99 } }
```

Choose one structure and apply it consistently.

